ongside Tennessee Williams in his own play.","displaySummary":"The Warhol superstar and transgender icon Candy Darling was glamour personified, but she was without a real place in the world. Growing up on Long Island, lonely and quiet and queer, she was enchanted by Hollywood starlets like Kim Novak. She found her turn in New York’s early Off-Off-Broadway theater scene, in Warhol’s films Flesh and Women in Revolt, and at the famed nightclub Max’s Kansas City. She inspired songs by Lou Reed and the Rolling Stones. She became friends with Jane Fonda and Lily Tomlin, borrowed a dress from Lauren Hutton, posed for Richard Avedon, and performed alongside Tennessee Williams in his own play.","primaryTopic":"Activist Biography","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Biography","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Biography","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Biography","mappedSubject":"Biography","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book provides a detailed life story of Candy Darling, emphasizing her significance as a queer icon and her cultural impact, making Biography the dominant subject with critical connections to Gender & Sexuality and Society & Culture.","id":"subject-evidence-book-candy-darling-dreamer-icon-superstar-cynthia-carr-1"},{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","rawLabel":"Biography & Autobiography","mappedSubject":"Memoir & Autobiography","score":7,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-candy-darling-dreamer-icon-superstar-cynthia-carr","id":"subject-evidence-book-candy-darling-dreamer-icon-superstar-cynthia-carr-6"},{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","rawLabel":"Biography & Autobiography","mappedSubject":"Biography","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-candy-darling-dreamer-icon-superstar-cynthia-carr","id":"subject-evidence-book-candy-darling-dreamer-icon-superstar-cynthi